������\n�\n���������",
    "ls|LS17_S8_U_125": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY \nDEPARTMENT OF SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No. U125 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 02.02.2022 \n \nSAFFORN BOWL PROJECT \n \n125. SHRI VINCENT H. PALA: \n \nWill the Minister of SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the status of extension of Saffron Bowl project to North Eastern Region \n(NER) by North East Centre for Technology Application & Reach (NECTAR); \n(b) the amount of funds allocated and sanctioned to Barapani (Meghalaya); \n(c) whether more sites have been identified in Meghalaya under the \nproject; \n(d) if so, the details thereof; and  \n(e) if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) OF THE  \nMINISTRY OF SCIENCE & TECHNOLOGY & EARTH SCIENCES \n(DR JITENDRA SINGH) \n \n(a) North East Centre for Technology Application and Reach (NECTAR) \nunder Saffron Bowl project has identified few locations in Arunachal \nPradesh and Meghalaya for saffron cultivation. In Arunachal Pradesh, there \nis a good growth of organic saffron with flowers. In Meghalaya, sample \nplantations were grown at Cherrapunji, Mosmoi and Lalingtop sites.  \n \n(b)  The total cost of the whole project is Rs. 17.68 lakhs for Arunachal \nPradesh and Meghalaya. Out of which, a tentative amount of Rs.6.00 lakhs \nhas been earmarked for Barapani (Meghalaya) site. \n \n(c) & (d) The following sites have been identified in Meghalaya under the \nsaid project: \ni. Barapani,  \nii. Cherrapunji,  \niii. Mosmoi,  \niv. Shillong and  \nv. Lalingtop. \n \n(e)  Does not arise. \n \n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S8_U_126": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 126 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON FEBRUARY 10, 2022 \n \nDEVELOPMENT OF SMART CITIES \n \nNO. 126.  SHRI Y.S. AVINASH REDDY: \n          ADV. ADOOR PRAKASH: \n \nWill the Minister of HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS be pleased to \n state: \n \n(a)  the total number of projects under the Smart C ities Mission  which have \nbeen completed and the total number of  projects  for  which work \norders were issued as on 31st December, 2021; \n \n(b)  the quantum of funds released as of December 2 021, out of the  total \ncommitment made by the Union Government to spend Rs.  48,000 \ncrore over a period of five years; \n \n(c)  the status of the execution of the work for de velopment of smart  cities \nin the country particularly in the States of Andhra Pradesh  and \nTelangana; \n \n(d)  whether any review has been conducted on the p ace of  execution \nof the said projects and if so, the details thereof ; and \n \n(e)  the steps being taken by the Union Government to expedite the \n completion of smart city projects in the country? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF  HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n \n(SHRI HARDEEP SINGH PURI) \n \n(a)  to (e):  A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.  \n***** \n\nSTATEMENT \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY OF PARTS (a) to (e) OF THE LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. *126 (6 TH POSITION) FOR ANSWER ON \n10.02.2022 REGARDING DEVELOPMENT OF SMART CITIES. \n \n(a) to (e):   Government of India launched the Smart Cities Missi on (SCM) on \n25 June 2015.  100 Smart cities have been selected through 4 rounds of \ncompetition from January 2016 to June 2018.   As pe r SCM Guidelines, \nCentral Government will provide financial support t o the extent of \u0001 48,000 \ncrore over five years i.e. on an average \u0001 100 crore per city per year.  An \nequal amount on a matching basis will be contribute d by the State \nGovernment/Urban Local Body.  As on 21 January 2022 , Government of India \nhas released \u0001 \u0001 28,413.60 crore for 100 Smart Cities, out of which  23,668.27 \ncrore (83%) have been utilized.   \n \nSo far, these Smart Cities have tendered out 6,721 projects worth        \u0001 \n1,88,506 crore; work orders have been issued in 6,1 24 projects worth \u0001 \n1,62,908 crore; 3,421 projects worth \u0001 58,735 crore have been completed.  \nState-wise/city-wise progress of projects of Smart Cities, including Smart \nCities of Andhra Pradesh and Telangana, is given in Annexure-I. \n \nThe implementation of SCM at the city level is done  by a Special Purpose \nVehicle (SPV) created for the purpose.  At State le vel, Mission \nimplementation is coordinated by the State level Hi gh Powered Steering \nCommittee (HPSC) chaired by the Chief Secretary of the State.   At the \nNational level, implementation of SCM is monitored by an Apex Committee \nheaded by Secretary, Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs (MoHUA).  \nNominee Directors of MoHUA on the Boards of SPVs mo nitor progress in \nrespective cities on a regular basis.  MoHUA regula rly interacts with the \nStates/Smart Cities through video conferences, revi ew meetings, field visits, \nregional workshops etc. at various levels to assess  the performance of cities \nand handhold them for improving the same. Smart Cit ies are assessed on \nvarious parameters including, but not limited to, p roject implementation and \nutilization of funds through the Online Geospatial Management Information \nSystem (GMIS). \nThe period of implementation of SCM has been extend ed upto June 2023 and \nall Smart Cities are expected to complete their pro jects within the stipulated \ntime.  \n**** \n  \n\nAnnexure-I in reply to parts (a) to (e) of Lok Sabh a Starred Question No. *126 for answer on \n10.02.2022 regarding Development of Smart Cities as ked by Shri Y.S. Avinash Reddy and Adv. \nAdoor Prakash, Hon’ble MPs.  \nState-wise/City-wise progress of projects of Smart Cities \n(Amount in ₹ crore) \nState/City \nDPR Stage Tender Stage Work Order Stage Work Completed Total \nNo. of \nProjects  Amount No. of \nProjects  Amount No. of \nProjects  Amount No. of \nProjects  Amount No. of \nProjects Amount \nAndaman Nicobar Islands 10 355.50  4 221.67  5 367.25  7 39.65  26  984.07  \nPort Blair 10 355.50  4 221.67  5 367.25  7 39.65  26  984.07  \nAndhra Pradesh 3 9.80  4 74.20  124  5788.89  138  1885.03  269  7757.92  \nAmaravati 0 0.00  0 0.00  21  2046.00  0 0.00  21  2046.00  \nKakinada 3 9.80  3 22.20  33  891.62  60  1015.37  99  1938.99  \nTirupati 0 0.00  0 0.00  53  1506.29  34  189.41  87  1695.70  \nVisakhapatnam 0 0.00  1 52.00  17  1344.98  44  680.25  62  2077.23  \nArunachal Pradesh 41 1733.11  6 202.17  13  96.11  11  187.10  71  2218.49  \nItanagar 18 683.68  1 19.52  5 81.14  4 92.79  28  877.13  \nPasighat 23 1049.43  5 182.65  8 14.97  7 94.31  43  1341.36  \nAssam 1 2.60  12  901.60  5 54.96  6 52.57  24  1011.73  \nGuwahati 1 2.60  12  901.60  5 54.96  6 52.57  24  1011.73  \nBihar 30 546.91  16  1203.29  72  3963.75  53  1428.30  171  7142.25  \nBhagalpur 7 5.00  5 474.28  18  1475.24  2 17.08  32  1971.60  \nBiharsharif 9 207.67  4 389.38  12  583.22  32  658.26  57  1838.53  \nMuzaffarpur 10 175.00  2 37.65  21  960.14  5 45.62  38  1218.41  \nPatna 4 159.24  5 301.98  21  945.15  14  707.34  44  2113.71  \nChandigarh 1 591.57  6 9.38  45  1855.81  29  305.20  81  2761.96  \nChandigarh 1 591.57  6 9.38  45  1855.81  29  305.20  81  2761.96  \nChhattisgarh 83 4405.78  69  1050.07  154  1809.18  149  958.52  455  8223.55  \nAtal Nagar 45 1365.16  3 32.64  17  331.35  2 163.91  67  1893.06  \nBilaspur 32 2547.30  19  317.46  31  1270.39  17  112.01  99  4247.16  \nRaipur 6 493.32  47  699.97  106  207.44  130  682.60  289  2083.33  \nDadra and Nagar Haveli 12 148.65  20  274.46  20  755.52  3 128.90  55  1307.53  \nSilvassa 12 148.65  20  274.46  20  755.52  3 128.90  55  1307.53  \nDaman and Diu 23 41