    "ls|LS17_S8_U_127": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 127 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 02.02.2022 \n \nDEATHS OF ELEPHANTS ON TRACKS \n \n127.  SHRI KARTI P. CHIDAMBARAM: \n  \n Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether  the Government is cognizant of the deficiencies in the \nprovision of Elephant Passages in Indian Railways as presented in \nthe CAG Report No.5 of 2021; \n \n(b) if so, whether the Railways has taken steps towards \nimplementing any of the suggestions detailed by the CAG in the \nreport to bridge these deficiencies for preventing Elephant deaths \non rail tracks;  \n \n(c) if so, the details thereof; and   \n \n(d) if not, the reasons therefor? \n \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND \nELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n \n(SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW) \n \n \n(a) to (d): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n***** \n \n \n \n \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 127 BY SHRI KARTI P. CHIDAMBARAM \nTO BE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 02.02.2022 REGARDING \nDEATHS OF ELEPHANTS ON TRACKS \n \n(a) to (d) Yes, Sir. Railways have already taken steps to prevent the \ndeaths of elephant on railway tracks in line with recommendations \nmade in Comptroller and Auditor General of India report no. 5 of \n2021.   \n \nA Permanent Co -ordination Committee has been constit uted \nbetween Ministry of Railways and Ministry of Environment, Forest \nand Climate Change for preventing elephant death in train \naccidents. Steps taken by Railways in coordination with Ministry of \nEnvironment, Forest and Climate Change to prevent accidental  \ndeath of elephants due to train hits are as follows:  \n(i) Imposition of speed restrictions in identified vulnerable locations. \n(ii) Providing signage boards at suitable points to alert train drivers \nabout elephant presence.   \n(iii) Sensitization of Train Crew and Station Masters on a regular \nbasis.  \n(iv) Clearing of vegetation along railway tracks to allow unhindered \nand clear view for train drivers. \n(v) Provision of fencing at selected locations. \n(vi) Avoid  dumping of food waste along railway track to avoid \nunnecessary congregation of elephants and other wild animals near \nrailway track.  \n(vii) Installation of innovative Honey bee sound systems at \nlocations, which are prone to crossing of elephants. \n***** \n ",
