    "ls|LS17_S8_U_25": " \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION No. *25 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 03rd FEBRUARY, 2022 \nROADMAP FOR ETHANOL BLENDING \n \n*25. SHRI CHANDRA PRAKASH CHOUDHARY: \n \nपे\u0000ो\u0000लयम  और \u0000ाक ृ \u0000तक गैस मं\u0000ी    \n \nWill the Minister of PETROLEUM AND NATURAL GAS be pleased to state:       \n(a) whether the Government has announced a roadmap for ethanol blending of fuel in \nthe country; \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n(c) whether the Government is aware of the impact of compatibility with ethanol fuels \nof on-road vehicles which are not designed/developed to run on 20 per cent ethanol \nblended fuel; \n(d) if so, whether it would result in increased fuel consumption and higher maintenance \ncosts of vehicles; and \n(e) whether the Government is taking any steps to address the issue and if so, the details \nthereof? \nANSWER \nisVªksfy;e vkSj izkÑfrd xSl ea=h \n (\u0000ी  हरद\u0000प \u0000संह पुर\u0000) \nMINISTER OF PETROLEUM & NATURAL GAS  \n (SHRI HARDEEP SINGH PURI) \n(a) to (e): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n****** \n \n  \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) TO (e) OF THE LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. *25 TO BE ANSWERED ON 03.02.2022 \nREGARDING ROADMAP FOR ETHANOL BLENDING BY SHRI CHANDRA \nPRAKASH CHOUDHARY \n(a) & (b): Government has been implementing Ethanol Blended Petrol (EBP) \nProgramme, wherein, Oil Marketing Companies (OMCs) sell petrol blended with \nethanol up to 10%. Due to several supply and demand side interventions since 2014, \nethanol blending quantity has significantly improved from 38 crore litre in Ethanol \nSupply Year (ESY – period from December to November) 2013-14 to 302.3 crore litre \nin ESY 2020-21. The average ethanol blending percentage has also increased from \n1.53% to 8.1% in the corresponding period. \nEncouraged by the past 7 years performance, Government decided to advance the target \nof 20% ethanol blending in petrol from 2030 to 2025. A Roadmap for Ethanol Blending \nin India 2020-25 was prepared by an inter-Ministerial Committee and placed in public \ndomain on World Environment Day i.e. on 5 th June, 2021. This roadmap provides \nguidance to achieve the target of 20% ethanol blending in petrol by bringing all \nstakeholders together i.e. Ethanol producers, Oil Companies, Vehicle manufacturers and \nConsumers.   \n(c) to (e): A joint study was undertaken by Indian Institute of Petroleum (IIP) \nDehradun, Automotive Research Association of India (ARAI) Pune and Indian Oil \nCorporation Limited (IOCL) R&D on E20 as fuel with existing vehicles under the aegis \nof Department of heavy Industry (DHI). Subsequently, BIS has issued specification for \nE20 fuel. Based on the study, Ministry of Road Transport and Highways (MoRTH) \nrecommended to adopt E20 fuel in the compatible vehicles as per Automotive Industry \nStandards (AIS) – 171. \n****** ",
    "ls|LS17_S8_U_26": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF MINORITY AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *26 \nANSWERED ON 03.02.2022 \n \nNAI ROSHNI SCHEME \n \n \n*26. SHRI TALARI RANGAIAH:  \nSHRIMATI VANGA GEETHA VISWANATH: \n  \nWill the Minister of MINORITY AFFAIRS be pleased to state : \n \n (a) the details of funds sanctioned under the Nai Roshni Scheme during the \nlast three years, State-wise; \n (b)  the details of funds utilized, out of the allocated funds, during the said \nperiod;  \n(c)  the details of physical and financial progress made so far under the said \nscheme; and  \n(d)  whether the Government has taken steps to ensure that beneficiaries have \nattained socio economic empowerment post training under the scheme and \nif so, the details thereof?  \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF MINORITY AFFAIRS \n(SHRI MUKHTAR ABBAS NAQVI) \n \n(a) to (d) :  A statement is laid on the table of the House. \n  \n\nStatement referred to in reply to Parts (a) to (d) of LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO. *26 asked by SHRI TALARI RANGAIAH and SHRIMATI VANGA \nGEETHA VISWANATH regarding “NAI ROSHNI SCHEME”. \n \n(a) to (d) : Nai Roshni scheme is a Central Sector scheme which aims to empower \nand enhance confidence in women by providing knowledge, tools and techniques for \nLeadership Development of Women.    \n  \nIt is a six-day non-residential/five-day residential training programme conducted by \nselected Programme Implementing Agencies for the women belonging to minority \ncommunity in the age group of 18 to 65 years. The training programme cover areas \nrelated to programmes for women, health and hygiene, legal rights of women, \nfinancial literacy, digital literacy, Swachch Bharat, Life Skills, and advocacy for social \nand behavioral changes, etc. Scheme-specific other detailed information is available \nat website http://nairoshni-moma.gov.in . The scheme provides for hand-holding of \nall the beneficiaries for a period upto 12 months after the training.  \n \nDuring the last three year i.e. 2018-19 to 2020-21, funds to the tune of Rs. 26 crores \nhave been sanctioned under the scheme through which around one Lakh women \nhave been trained. State-wise details of physical and financial progress for the last \nthree years is placed at Annexure. \n \nSo far, Rs.108.24 Crore have been released to the Programme Implementing \nAgencies and around 4.35 Lakh women have been trained under the scheme. \n \n \n***** \n  \n\nANNEXURE  \n \nAnnexure referred to in reply to Parts (a) to (d) of LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO. *26 asked by SHRI TALARI RANGAIAH and SHRIMATI VANGA \nGEETHA VISWANATH regarding “NAI ROSHNI SCHEME”. \n \nState-wise details of funds sanctioned under the Nai Roshni Scheme during \nthe last three years (2018-19 to 2020-21) \n \nS. \nNo. \nStates Fund Released  \n(in Rs. crores) \n1 Andhra Pradesh 0.39 \n2 Arunachal Pradesh 0.03 \n3 Assam 1.34 \n4 Bihar 0.14 \n5 Chhattisgarh 0.14 \n6 Delhi 0.59 \n7 Gujarat 0.03 \n8 Haryana 0.51 \n9 Himanchal Pradesh 0.03 \n10 Jammu & Kashmir 0.30 \n11 Jharkhand 0.12 \n12 Karnataka 0.29 \n13 Kerala 0.16 \n14 Madhya Pradesh 3.11 \n15 Maharashtra 0.50 \n16 Meghalaya 0.02 \n17 Nagaland 0.08 \n18 Odisha 0.15 \n19 Punjab 0.29 \n20 Rajasthan 1.08 \n21 Telangana 0.13 \n22 Tamil Nadu 0.22 \n23 Uttar Pradesh 15.91 \n24 Uttarakhand 0.65 \n25 West Bengal 0.47 \n ",
