    "ls|LS17_S8_U_34": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO . 34 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON FEBRUARY 03, 2022 \n \nCONSTRUCTION OF HOUSES UNDER PMAY-U \nNO.  34.     SHRI VIJAYAKUMAR (ALIAS) VIJAY VASANTH: \n  SHRI THIRUNAVUKKARASAR SU: \nWill the Minister of HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n(a) the number of houses/flats sanctioned/construct ed in the country for \nurban poor under Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana (PMAY-U ) during the \nlast three years, year and State-wise particularly in the State of Tamil \nNadu; \n(b) whether delay in construction of the same resul ts in huge cost \nescalation and if so, the details thereof; \n(c) whether a large number of houses constructed un der the scheme are \nlying vacant;  \n(d) if so, the details of allotments made and vacant flats, State-wise;  \n(e) whether the Government has taken any steps for early allotment of \nvacant flats under the scheme to eligible beneficiaries; and \n(f) if so, the details thereof and the time by whic h the vacant flats are \nlikely to be allotted? \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF  HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n \n(SHRI HARDEEP SINGH PURI) \n \n(a) to (f) A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n....2/- \n \n\n \n \n-2- \nSTATEMENT \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA STARRED  \nQUESTION NO. 34* (14 th  POSITION) FOR ANSWER ON 03.02.2022 \nREGARDING “CONSTRUCTION OF HOUSES UNDER PMAY-U”. \n \n(a) The State/ UT wise number of houses sanctioned and \nconstructed/completed, including the State of Tamil  Nadu, during the last \nthree years under Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana- Urban  (PMAY-U) is at \nAnnexure-I.  Out of 1.14 crore houses sanctioned un der PMAY-U, around \n54.4 lakh houses are complete and the remaining hou ses are at various \nstages of construction/grounding.   \n(b) Under PMAY-U, Government of India is sanctionin g the proposals \nbased on the Detailed Project Reports (DPRs) along with project cost \nprepared by the implementing agencies of States/UTs . Government of \nIndia is providing its fixed share as Central Assis tance of \n\u00011.0 lakh under \nIn-Situ Slum Redevelopment (ISSR), \u00011.5 lakh for Affordable Housing in \nPartnership (AHP) & Beneficiary-led individual hous e construction or \nenhancement (BLC) verticals of PMAY-U. The remainin g cost of the house \nas per DPR is shared by States/UTs/ULBs/Beneficiari es. Completion of \nprojects generally takes 12-36 months under differe nt verticals of the \nscheme.  Any cost escalation, due to delay in construction or otherwise is \nborne by State/ UTs/ ULBs/ beneficiaries as per DPR . Under Pradhan \nMantri Awas Yojana – Urban [PMAY-U], identification  of eligible \nbeneficiaries, implementation of projects including  completion of houses, \nallotment to beneficiaries and ensuring occupancy b y providing all \nnecessary infrastructure is the responsibility of States/UTs.   \n(c)& (d) No Sir. Out of 54,39,898 houses constructe d so far under \nPMAY-U, only 5,76,735 houses are yet to be occupied .  State/UT wise \ndetails of number of houses constructed and houses in the process of \nallotment/ occupancy is at Annexure-II.   \n(e) & (f) In order to achieve the vision of ‘Housin g for All’, Ministry \nmonitors progress of the Scheme through periodic re view meetings, \nvideo-conferences and field visits.  Ministry, at v arious fora such as \nReview meetings, Workshops/ Conferences, Central Sa nctioning & \nMonitoring Committee (CSMC) meetings etc., and thro ugh \ncorrespondences, has advised States/ UTs to expedite the construction of \nsanctioned  houses so that all houses are completed within the stipulated \nperiod and allotted to eligible beneficiaries.   \n***** \n\n \nAnnexure-I \n \n Annexure-I referred in reply to Lok Sabha Starred Q.No.34 for 03-02-2022  \n \nStates/UTs  wise  details  of  houses  sanctioned  and constructed during the last three years  \nUnder PMAY-U \nAs on 24.01.2022  \nSr. \nN