    "ls|LS17_S8_U_68": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF TOURISM \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.*68 \nANSWERED ON 07.02.2022 \n \nTRIBAL TOURISM IN MEGHALAYA \n \n*68.  SHRI VINCENT H. PALA: \n \n  Will the Minister of TOURISM be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Ministry has undertaken any a ction plan to encourage \nTribal Tourism in Meghalaya post-Pandemic; \n(b) if so, the details of the steps taken and the tribes considered for such \nan endeavour; \n(c) the details of the steps taken to promote tribal culture of North \nEastern Region (NER) and Meghalaya in particular; \n(d) the details of tourists in NER during the last five years, State and \nyear-wise; and \n(e) the investment made in Tourism Sector in NER during the last five \nyears, State and year-wise? \n \n ANSWER \nMINISTER OF TOURISM     (SHRI G. KISHAN REDDY) \n \n \n(a) to ( e) : A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n***** \n \n \n \n \n\n \nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (e) O F LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO. *68 ANSWERED ON 07.02.2022 REGARDING TRIBAL \nTOURISM IN MEGHALAYA. \n  \n(a)   to (c):  Yes, Sir. The Min istry of Tourism promotes India as a holistic \ntourist destination including tribal tourism in Meghalaya under the \n“Incredible India” brand and promotional activities are undertaken in \nDomestic and International markets through its various schemes such as \nDomestic Promotion & Publicity including Hospitality (DPPH) and Overseas \nPromotion & Publicity including Market Development Assistance (OPMD) \nwithout distinction of any tribe. \n  \nPost Pandemic, digital promotions are regularly undertaken through the \nSocial Media accounts of the Ministry on different themes such as heritage \ntourism, tribal tourism, culture tourism, amongst others. Webinars  are \norganised under the overall “Dekho Apna Desh” theme  showcasing the \ndiverse culture, heritage, destinations and tourism products of the country, \nincluding North  East India. The details of webinars being organized \nfocusing on NER   under this series include:  Cruising the Brahmaputra \nRiver, the World’s Greatest Natural History & Heritage River Cruise, \nAdventure tourism in NE India, Bailey Trail in Arunachal Pradesh, Northeast \nIndia for the immersive traveler, Northeast India: Experience the exclusive \nvillages, Assamese Cuisine- The Gourmet Unexplored, Mystique Nagaland – \nLand of Culture, Adventure and Festivals. \n  \nNew initiat ive has been made named Prime Minister’s Development \nInitiative for North  East, (PM -DevINE) to enable livelihood activities for \nyouth and women and filling the gaps in various sectors that will also help \ntourism growth in North Eastern Region (NER). \n  \nDetails of steps taken in this regard are placed at Annexure I. \n  \n(d):  The details of tourists in NER during the last five years,  State and \nyear-wise is at Annexure II. \n  \n(e): The investment made in Tourism Sector by the Ministry in NER during \nthe last five years, State and year-wise is at Annexure III. \n  \n***** \n\nANNEXURE I \n \nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) to (c) OF LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO.*68 ANSWERED ON 07.02.2022 REGARDING TRIBAL \nTOURISM IN MEGHALAYA \n \nDETAILS OF STEPS TAKEN TO PROMOTE  TRIBAL CULTURE IN  NORTH \nEASTERN REGION AND MEGHALAYA \n \n1. Training was conducted for tribal participants from Border Areas of \ndifferent Districts of Meghalaya so as to promote the Tribal Cuisine of \nMeghalaya. After completion of the course each participant has been \nsupported with a set of Start -Up asset in order to promote Tribal \nTourism through Tribal Cuisine of Meghalaya and also to encourage \nthe mitigation of migration of the Tribals from the Rural areas. \n \n2. Culinary Videos was created to Showcase the Cultural Significan ce \nand Diversities of Ethnic Foods of all Northeastern States of India and \nto promote Tribal Tourism. Through these Culinary Videos we have \nmade efforts to showcase the creativity and treasure of food heritage \nof tribals of all the North Eastern States of India including Sikkim . \nThrough these Culinary Videos we have made efforts to bring \nawareness about the cuisines of the frontier States of North East \nIndia and to showcase the indigenous cuisine and also to collect all \nthe unique recipes and preserve them for generations to come and \nmake the world aware of our unique culinary heritage and thus \npromoting the Tribal Tourism. \n \n3. ‘Start-up’ in the field of catering services and food joints under \nentrepreneurship programme were conducted. The Training Program \nwas conducted for 1 (One) batch of 30 (Thirty) Tribal participants \nfrom all the North-East States of India. After completion of the course \neach participant has been supported with a set of Start -Up asset in \norder to promote the spirit of Entrepreneurship am ong the tribals of \nNorth East India and so as to encourage the mitigation of migration of \nthe Tribals from the Rural areas and thus promoting the Tribal \nTourism. \n \n4. Further various Awareness Programs, Traditional Walks, Fashion \nShows, Food Festivals and o ther related events in order to promote \nTribal Tourism and to showcase the Cultural Significance and \nDiversities of all Northeastern States of India have been taken. \n \n\n5. Steps were taken by  North East Zonal Culture Centre (NEZCC) to \npromote tribal culture of the North East ern States, including \nMeghalaya. Which, inter-alia, included:   \n  \n Bharat Ko Janno (Cultural  Exchange Programme between NE \nStates and other States) \n Border Area Programme (International Borders) \n Women Activities Programmes (Skill development workshops) \n Documentation of Vanishing Art forms \n Guru Shishya Parampara \n Young Talent Artist Awards \n Stone Sculpture Workshops \n Wood Carving Workshops \n Painting Workshops \n Theatre Rejuvenation (Workshops) \n Umang for differently abled children (Workshops) \n Bridging Folk & Classical Dance \n Tribal Visual Arts Workshops cum Exhibition \n Celebration of Important Tribal Festival \n Traditional Tribal Food Festival \n• Guru shishya parampara scheme (19 guiruso last 5 years till \ndate) \n• Documentation of vanishing art forms  \n  \nOctave (Festivals showcasing the tribal art/culture/cuisine/ \ncrafts/costumes of North East) are held every year by every Zonal \nCentre in states other than the North Eastern States. \n \nThe tribal communities of the 8 North Eastern States are promoted \nthrough pro grammes by NEZCC at important festivals such as \nHornbill (Nagaland), Sangei (Manipur), Shilpagram Utsav (Assam) etc. \n \nTribal crafts of the NE are sold through several exhibitions at all \nmajor festivals and crafts fairs across the country. \n \n6. Fairs & festivals funded by Ministry of Tourism: \n(Rs. In Lakh) \nName of \nState \nYear  Name of Fairs & Festivals Amount \nsanctioned \nAssam 2014-15 0 0 \n 2015-16 0 0 \n 2016-17 CFA for Celebration of (i) Rass \nMahotsav, Majuli (ii) Bodo National \n35.00 \n\nFestival (iii) Rongali Festival \n 2017-18 0 0 \n 2018-19 International Buddhist conference 25.00 \n  CFA for organizing Rongali festival 25.00 \n 2021-22 Bhogali Festival 25.00 \nArunachal \nPradesh \n2014-15 Celebration of Nyokum Festival 14.00 \n 2015-16 (i) Kameng River Eco-Tourism \nFestival (ii) Menchuka Adventure \nFestival and (iii) Orange Festival \nDambuk \n30.00 \n 2016-17 0 0 \n 2017-18 (i) Tawang Festival  \n(ii)Menchuka Adventure Festival  \n(iii) Orange Festival Dambuk \n40.00 \n 2018-19 Basar Confluence 3.0 Festival 20.00 \n 2019-20 CFA for organizing River Tribe’s \nAngling Festival & Butterfly Meet at \nMIAO \n50.00 \n 2020-21 Organizing Pedal to Pakke 25.00 \n 2021-22 Easterly Essence Ledum Festival & \nOrange Festival of Music and \nAdventure  \n50.00 \n 2019-20 National Tribal Festival 20.00 \nManipur 2014-15 Manipuri Festival and Youth, \nAdventure& Water sports festival \n50.00 \n 2015-16 Manipur Sangai Festival and Youth