    "ls|LS17_S8_U_99": "O.I.H.\n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF COOPERATION\n \n \nLOK SABHA\n \nSTARRED QUESTION N\nO\n. 99\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON \n8\nTH\n \nFEBRUARY 2022\n \n \nMULTI\n-\nPURPOSE COOPERATIVE SOCIETIES\n \n \n*99. \n \nSHRI HANUMAN BENIWAL:\n \n \nWill the \nMinister o\nf \nCOOPERATION\n \nसहका\u0000रता\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \nbe pleased to \nstate:\n \n \n(a) \n \nwhether the Government is aware that multi\n-\npurpose cooperative societies set up \nin various Statesof the country, including Rajasthan have mis\n-\nappropriated\n \ncrores of \nrupees of investors;\n \n(b)\n \nif\n \nso, the number of such cases which have cometo the notice of the \nGovernment;\n \n(c)\n \nthe amount of money mis\n-\napproriated by the said\n \nsocieties alongwith the number \nof investors who lost\n \ntheir money in the process, society\n-\nwise; and\n \n(d) \n \nthe steps taken by the\n \nGovernment in this regard\n \nto safeguard the interest of the \ninvestors?\n \n \nANSWER\n \nMINISTER OF COOPERATION\n \nसहका\u0000रता\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \n(SHRI\n \n \nAMIT SHAH\n)\n \n \n(a) to (d\n): A statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (\nd\n) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. \n99\n \nDUE FOR REPLY ON \n8\nTH\n \nFEBRUARY, 2022\n \n \n(a) \nto\n \n(d) Yes sir. A large number of complaints have be\nen received for non\n-\nrepayment / \nmisappropriation of deposits of investors against some of the multi\n-\nstate cooperative \nsocieties in various states of the Country, including Rajasthan. In case of delinquent \nsocieties against whom complaints are received, action for winding up is taken unde\nr \nSection 86 of the Multi\n-\nState Cooperative Societies (MSCS) Act, 2002.  Presently \nwinding up proceedings is underway in case of 77 societies, a list of which is at \nAnnexure A.\n \nComplete details regarding the amount of money misappropriated by the \nsocieties\n, along with the numbers of members who lost their money is not available.\n \n\nAnnexure\n-\nA\n \nList of multi\n-\nState cooperative societies against whom liquidation proceedings \nare under way under Section 86 of the MSCS Act, 2002:\n \nSl. \nNo.\n \nName of the society\n \nState\n \n1\n.\n \n \nJatropha Growers & Bio\n-\nFuel Development Cooperative \nLtd., Hyderabad, Andhra Pradesh\n \nAndhra \nPradesh\n \n2\n.\n \n \nThe Regional Resource Development Cooperative Society \nLtd., Vijayawada, Andhra Pradesh\n \nAndhra \nPradesh\n \n3\n.\n \n \nSouth Indian Fisherman Coop. Society Ltd., \nVishakap\natnam, A.P.\n \nAndhra \nPradesh\n \n4\n.\n \n \nGrahak Bazar Cooperative Society Ltd., Hyderabad, \nAndhra Pradesh\n \nAndhra \nPradesh\n \n5\n.\n \n \nTourism Development Coop. India Ltd., Jangpura, New \nDelhi\n \nDelhi\n \n6\n.\n \n \nJyoti Credit & Savings SwablambiSahakariSamiti Ltd., \nMathura Road, New Delhi\n \nDelhi\n \n7\n.\n \n \nSkylark Multi\n-\nState Cooperative Group Housing Society \nLtd., PaschimVihar, New Delhi\n \nDelhi\n \n8\n.\n \n \nCrown Credit Coopertaive Society Ltd., Dwarka, Delhi\n \nDelhi\n \n9\n.\n \n \nSuccess Valley Credit Cooperative Society Ltd., \nShakarpur, Delhi\n \nDelhi\n \n10\n.\n \n \nCooperative Store \nLtd., Super Bazar, New Delhi\n \nDelhi\n \n11\n.\n \n \nHBN Credit Cooperative Society Ltd., PashimVihar, New \nDelhi\n \nDelhi\n \n12\n.\n \n \nLokhitBharti Credit Cooperative Society Ltd., ShivajiMarg, \nNew Delhi\n \nDelhi\n \n13\n.\n \n \nAadi Credit Cooperative Society Ltd., New Delhi\n \nDelhi\n \n14\n.\n \n \nEye Vision India Credit Cooperative Society Ltd., New \nDelhi\n \n\nDelhi\n \n15\n.\n \n \nMapusa Urban Cooperative Bank of Goa Ltd., Goa\n \nGoa\n \n16\n.\n \n \nGujarat Industrial Cooperative Bank Limited, Ahmedabad\n \nGujarat\n \n17\n.\n \n \nMadhavpura Mercantile Cooperative Bank Limited, \nAhmedabad\n \nGujarat\n \n18\n.\n \n \nPetrofils Cooperative Ltd. Vadodara, Gujarat\n \nGujarat\n \n19\n.\n \n \nAdarsh Credit Cooperative Society Ltd., Ahmedaba